cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "microfinance-fraud-detection: catching a loan-repayment skimming scheme in a synthetic portfolio"
message: "If you use this code or method, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Baah
    given-names: Samuel Ato Kwame
    affiliation: "Independent researcher, Accra, Ghana"
    email: samatohobbs@gmail.com
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0002-8773-7525"
abstract: >-
  SQL rules and Python anomaly detection applied to a synthetic 24-month microfinance loan book of
  3,000 borrowers, into which a loan-repayment skimming scheme is injected. The project reports
  what the detection misses as carefully as what it catches: the guilty officers are ranked first
  and second, while only a minority of the skimmed installments are identified, because an honest
  short payment and a skimmed one look identical one row at a time. Every record is synthetic and
  generated from a fixed seed.
keywords:
  - fraud detection
  - anomaly detection
  - forensic accounting
  - audit analytics
  - microfinance
  - synthetic data
  - reproducible research
license: MIT
